# Frontend UI consistency (jobwright dashboard)

## Skip gate

If this turn does **not** build, change, or polish dashboard UI (`frontend/`), ignore the rest of this rule.

If it does, **load** [.cursor/skills/frontend-tasteful/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/frontend-tasteful/SKILL.md) **before editing**. That skill holds the living catalog (primitives, tokens, little things). Do not invent a parallel inventory here.

## Reuse ladder (do not skip)

1. shadcn in `frontend/src/components/ui/` (default variants; do not fork inline).
2. Domain primitives in `frontend/src/components/` (see the skill catalog).
3. Tokens / classes in `frontend/src/index.css` (`:root`, `@layer components`).

Extend an existing primitive or token before adding a one-off. If the user still wants a new control, implement it once as a reusable component (or token + class), wire call sites, and **promote** it into the skill catalog in the same change.

## Do not

- Load global landing-page / portfolio taste skills (`design-taste-frontend`, Three Dials, heroes, airy marketing layouts) for this product.
- Leave one-off markup in `App.tsx` or page files when a shared primitive fits.
- Change behavior, data contracts, or accessibility to "fix" visuals.
- Duplicate lane/stage colors; use `laneTone()` / `--stage-*`.

## Promote

Update `.cursor/skills/frontend-tasteful/references/catalog.md` only when you add or rename a **reusable** domain component, add a **reusable** token/class family, or change a consistency convention. Skip copy tweaks, bugfixes, and page-local layout.
